  "scope_statement": {
    "macro_free_isolation": "Verifier runs in separate OS process reading only canonical flat 1-bit opcodes (ALLOC, FREE_ZERO, X, CX, Z, CZ, GLOBAL_Z, AND, MX_FREE) with strict EOF/reserved-bit enforcement; compiler holds zero quantum state and enforces an explicit operation allowlist.",
    "measurement_safety_precondition": "Sampled trajectory replay relies on R4B's structural MX-dependency theorem (Appendix B.1): every MX-measured wire holds a deterministic single-valued function of surviving computational-basis wires at measurement time, precluding branch merging.",
    "branch_and_history_coverage": "64 computational-basis input pairs under one shared seeded full-scale MX measurement history (SplitMix64 seed=2026111501): 62 independent random 1536-bit (x, m) pairs verified against both pow(3, x, N) CRT bounds AND exact 0-LSB truncated-CRT integer oracle mod N_trunc = 6,697,130,461 + 2 constructed D=26 overflow/underflow pairs verified for work-wire and phase cleanup. Three independent MX histories are tested at 79 primes.",
    "non_claims": "Does not prove arbitrary-input quantum-channel equivalence by trajectory sampling alone (rare D=26 tail weight p_bad <= 2.83e-10 is certified separately via 256-fractional-bit 512-term positive Taylor MGF bounds + logical-isometry factoring in Appendix C.6) and does not re-lower all 40 Pareto-frontier or 28 baseline circuits across 19,878 primes (Pareto curves remain matched primitive-cost-model comparisons)."
  },
